{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation evidence before review: CI-matched baseline focused runs were 56.82s, 55.72s, 56.22s (median 56.22s). Final runs were 29.24s, 29.93s, 29.31s (median 29.31s), saving 26.91s / 47.9% across the focused set and clearing the >=20s aggregate bar. Each modified family cleared 50%: lock windows now preserve the real holder, dual-window flock/mkdir, real production backoff, attempt/warning/body-replay assertions at 2.5x holder/pass scale; shutdown uses the same 60/40 shared-budget geometry and a real thread barrier; autodeploy injects persisted episode age and models down-old/healthy-replacement while dedicated health-gate tests retain unhealthy rollback. reviewbot ensure was intentionally not edited because its ~15s is real clone/fetch/reconvergence/ensure/write durability, not a clock window. Exact-defect mutations remained RED after shortening: retries disabled 2/2 failed; fresh drain plus no in-flight gate 2/2 failed; episode reset plus unknown-as-busy 2/2 failed. Final focused four-file suite: 142 passed in 51.42s. CI-shaped default: 13,582 passed, 17 skipped in 1089.09s; integration: 167 passed, 2 skipped in 114.11s; no phase exceeded 30s. make lint and make typecheck passed. Production files and defaults are unchanged. Discovered security follow-up broadish-permanent-condor after pytest demonstrated ambient fixture values can appear in failure output; it is linked and out of this change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786835076907748001,"uuid":"eba1f699-79ed-4545-b123-d1d138e3178e"}